<DocsLayout title="Capability matrix" description="The evidence boundary for each dataset modality in super-charge-ml." current="capabilities">
  <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Support boundary</p>
  <h1>Know what is<br /><em>actually supported.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead">A parser is not a production capability. A dataset family is supported only when ingestion, curation, modelling, evaluation, packaging, inference, monitoring, documentation, and recovery have evidence.</p>

  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Read the label literally.</strong> <code>supported</code> means the complete lifecycle is proven for the declared scope. <code>experimental</code> means you can explore it with explicit opt-in. <code>extension-only</code> means the integration boundary exists, but this beta makes no lifecycle guarantee.</p></div>

  <h2>Current beta matrix</h2>
  <p class="table-hint">On a narrow screen, scroll the matrix horizontally to read the full evidence boundary.</p>
  <div class="capability-table" role="region" aria-label="Capability support matrix" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Dataset family</th><th>Current label</th><th>What exists</th><th>What is missing</th></tr></thead>
